Subject: The poll of a frameless body builds the backtrace of the exception it raises

What this does
  - `qjs_aot_poll_fl` is `qjs_aot_poll` plus the backtrace of an exception the poll raised, built at
    the poll. Frameless bodies (the entry of a function with calls, the poll in a frameless loop, the
    pure recursive form) call it in place of `qjs_aot_poll`.

Why we need it
  The interrupt handler's "interrupted" error is thrown with its backtrace deferred to the unwinder of
  the catching frame, after the frameless activation records are popped (see 0373), so a function
  interrupted deep in a compiled recursion reported only the frame that caught it. The poll of a
  frameless body is always the innermost activation, so the backtrace can be built there.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -64217,6 +64217,18 @@
     return 0;
 }
 
+/* The poll of a frameless body, whose frame is only its activation record: an exception the
+   poll raises gets its backtrace here, while the records are in place (see
+   qjs_aot_throw_stack_overflow). */
+QJS_AOT_STUB int qjs_aot_poll_fl(JSContext *ctx)
+{
+    int rc = qjs_aot_poll(ctx);
+
+    if (unlikely(rc < 0) && needs_backtrace(ctx->rt->current_exception))
+        build_backtrace(ctx, ctx->rt->current_exception, JS_UNDEFINED, NULL, 0, 0, 0);
+    return rc;
+}
+
 QJS_AOT_STUB uint32_t qjs_aot_epoch(JSContext *ctx)
 {
     return ctx->rt->ic_watchpoint_epoch;
--- a/quickjs-aot-rt.h
+++ b/quickjs-aot-rt.h
@@ -234,6 +234,7 @@
    an interpreted one share the same budget. Returns 0 to continue, -1 after
    throwing. */
 QJS_AOT_STUB int qjs_aot_poll(JSContext *ctx);
+QJS_AOT_STUB int qjs_aot_poll_fl(JSContext *ctx);
 
 /* Sentinels returned by qjs_aot_step; they mirror REGVM_COLD_RET and
    REGVM_STEP_SUSPEND in quickjs.c. */
